question:
What does a unit test verify?
```javascript
describe('Math.add', () => {
  it('adds two numbers', () => {
    expect(Math.add(2, 3)).toBe(5);
  });
});
```

When should you mock dependencies?
```javascript
const fetchUser = jest.fn().mockResolvedValue({id: 1});
const user = await getUserById(1, fetchUser);
expect(fetchUser).toHaveBeenCalledWith(1);
```

What does test coverage measure?
```javascript
// 80% line coverage
if (user.admin) {
  // not tested
}
```

How should you test async functions?
```javascript
it('fetches user data', async () => {
  const user = await getUser(1);
  expect(user.id).toBe(1);
});
```

What does beforeEach hook do?
```javascript
beforeEach(() => {
  db.clearCache();
});
it('test 1', () => { /* runs after beforeEach */ });
it('test 2', () => { /* runs after beforeEach again */ });
```

How should you test error handling?
```javascript
it('throws on invalid input', () => {
  expect(() => parseInput('bad')).toThrow();
});
```

What does jest.spyOn do?
```javascript
const spy = jest.spyOn(console, 'log');
console.log('test');
expect(spy).toHaveBeenCalledWith('test');
spy.mockRestore();
```

How should you test HTTP endpoints?
```javascript
const request = require('supertest');
it('GET /users returns 200', async () => {
  const res = await request(app).get('/users');
  expect(res.status).toBe(200);
});
```

When should you use snapshot testing?
```javascript
it('renders UI', () => {
  const html = render(<Button />);
  expect(html).toMatchSnapshot();
});
```

What is the difference between describe and it?
```javascript
describe('User API', () => {
  it('fetches users', () => { /* test */ });
  it('creates user', () => { /* test */ });
});
```
